  "summary": "The Garment of Charity passes: the complete spoken body and all three proof pages were independently read, its relation to the study's two interpretations checked, and its claims tested against Missale Romanum 1962 pp. 411\u2013412, Augustine Sermon 90.4\u20136 and 9\u201310 and Psalm 118 Aleph 4\u20135, Gregory Homily 38.9\u201312, Chrysostom Ephesians XIV on 4:25\u201328, and Schuster III pp. 171\u2013174. The speech develops one clear, parish-level argument from the wedding garment through concrete charity to Eucharistic healing and hope; its independently counted 1,301 words support the stated 10.4\u201311.3-minute estimate at 115\u2013125 words per minute before additional pauses, with no audible rehearsal or timed human performance certified and no fresh print collation claimed for the retained patristic transcriptions or Schuster OCR."
